  "result": "I haven't changed any code yet. I'm in plan mode, so I only wrote the plan. I don't have a plan-approval tool here, so please tell me to proceed if you want me to implement it.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` splits the command line with `shlex`. `shlex` treats an unquoted `#` as the start of a comment and drops the rest of the line. The bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell completers all use it, so `args` and `incomplete` come out wrong. In fish it can also crash with an `IndexError`.\n\n**Fix:** set `lex.commenters = \"\"` in `split_arg_string`.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Add `#` cases to `tests/test_parser.py::test_split_arg_string`.\n- Add `#` cases to `test_full_complete` in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`.\n- Add a `CHANGES.md` entry.\n\nI haven't run `shlex` to confirm how it handles `a#b` (a `#` in the middle of a word). The new test cases will check that.\n\nThe plan is at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-floofy-eagle.md`.",
